The editor's daily work. Editors choose what to publish, read editing words instead of Git words, and see on every entry whether it is published. A form checks its fields while the editor types, keeps unsaved changes when the session ends, and shows both versions when two editors save the same entry. When the URL of an entry changes, the links to it can follow. Files can be deleted from the Media view, uploads stay with their entry, and a new content model is used without a restart.

## Breaking

A save no longer checks required fields; Publish does. Each publication's commit ends with a `Published-with: Mica` line. In the local editor, Publish waits while the branch holds other commits that are not pushed yet.

**Publish takes the chosen changes.** The Publish page has a checkbox for each change. A change comes with the new entries and files that it uses, and the rest stays saved. The staging status reports `unpushed: { mica, other }` instead of `ahead`.

**Required fields are checked at Publish, not at Save.** You can save a half-finished entry. The entry page says "Not ready to publish" and names the empty fields. A new entry needs a title or a URL.

**Mica marks its commits.** Each publication's commit ends with the trailer `Published-with: Mica`. In the local editor, Publish and its retry refuse while the branch holds commits that its upstream does not have and that Mica did not make. Push them, or move them to another branch.

**Uploads go into the entry's folder.** A file that you upload in an entry or settings form goes into its own `media/` folder. The picker offers the files of that folder and the shared files. Files that are already in the shared folder stay there. Videos are refused.

**Slugs and sorting are typed.** Mica reads the slug field of a collection from the file name of the entry and types it as `string`, never `null`. A second slug field among the own fields of a collection stops the build. `defaultSort.field` must be a field of the collection or `"position"`. The `coordinates` options `defaultCenter` and `defaultZoom` are removed.

**Validation messages name the field and the limit**, such as "Title can have at most 120 characters (now 134)." The unused `coordinatesSchema` export is removed.

**`findReferences` also returns settings pages**, as `{ kind: "entry" | "singleton", … }`.

**`restart_required` means only a `.gitattributes` change.** A new content model needs no restart.

## Added

**Delete in the Media view.** Mica deletes a file, or a selection, when no field and no rich text uses it. The view shows where a file is used. The delete waits on the Publish page, and Discard brings the file back.

**Links follow a URL change.** The entry page names the entries and settings pages that link to the entry. It offers to update their links in the same save.

**Save conflicts show both versions**, with "Keep mine" (the log names the editor) and "Use theirs".

**A new content model without a restart.** Mica loads it as soon as the manifest changes, in both apps. An open page asks the editor to save and load it again. If Mica cannot read the model, it keeps the old one, and the System and Publish pages say why.

**The end of a session keeps the work.** The page offers "Sign in again" and returns to the same place. Forms keep unsaved changes in the browser tab and offer to restore them. A warning comes five minutes before the end. Each response names the end of the session in `x-mica-session-expires`.

**`patternMessage`** on text fields, and a description for every builder option.

**`relinkReferences` and `mapMedia`** in `@micacms/core`.

**The log names the editor** for Publish, Discard, conflict choices, media deletes and "Keep mine".

## Changed

**Editing words, not Git words.** The editor says "Say what changed" instead of "commit message". Git details are only on the System page and in a closed "Details for developers" section.

**Publish state everywhere.** Entries and settings show "Saved · not published" with Publish and Discard. Lists mark new and changed entries, and each change shows when it was saved.

**The form checks fields in the browser** when the editor leaves them and before a save. Each problem links to its field, also from the Publish page.

**In `astro dev`, an unfinished draft is left out** with a warning, and the rest of the collection loads. A build still fails.

**Dependencies are refreshed.** The example site uses MapLibre 6 and sharp 0.35.

## Fixed

"Today" in a date field uses the local date. A half-typed coordinate is named as missing instead of 0. The list search no longer matches field names. List cells show dates, choices, rich text and files in a readable way. A settings page that fails to load no longer shows an empty form. `mica check` reads the slug as the file has it.
